### `common-includes.hcl` Tag Assembly

The `common` object is assembled in `common-includes.hcl` using a `merge()` of three tag locals. The following pattern is the approved implementation per STD-INFRA-IAC-003:

```hcl
# common-includes.hcl

locals {
  company_tags = {
    Company     = "Gainwell"
    Email       = "mmes-cms-mbr@gainwelltech.com"
    BillingCode = "CC-12345"
    Tenant      = "cm"
  }

  cloud_tags = {
    CloudProvider = "AWS"
    Account       = get_aws_account_alias()
  }

  env_tags = {
    Environment = local.env_short_name   # dev | test | sit | uat | prd
  }

  managed_by_tag = {
    ManagedBy = "terraform:${basename(get_terragrunt_dir())}"
  }

  common = {
    tags = merge(
      local.company_tags,
      local.cloud_tags,
      local.env_tags,
      local.managed_by_tag,
    )
  }
}
```

**Key rules for this pattern:**

- `get_aws_account_alias()` resolves the AWS account alias at plan time — no hardcoded account IDs.
- `basename(get_terragrunt_dir())` produces the deployment directory name as `<deployment_name>`, satisfying REQ-IAC-012-03.
- The merge order places `managed_by_tag` last so it cannot be overridden by earlier locals.
- All four tag group locals (`company_tags`, `cloud_tags`, `env_tags`, `managed_by_tag`) **must** be defined; none may be omitted.

